{"title":"Darkestest Secrets! There Will be Blood - Hosted by HH Holmes (RETURN FOR 2026)","startsAt":"2026-10-16T19:00:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-16T21:00:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nStart the fall season on a high note with this frightening walking tour hosted by **HH Holmes** the most prolific serial killer in American History. Considered the first serial killer he will conduct this entire tour from beginning to end. It will keep you up late at night for days.\n\nThis tour will be hosted and conducted by a man who committed some of the most vicious crimes, and there is a Toronto connection to it all. He loved Toronto and wished it well.\n\nFrom serial killers to strange disappearances, this tour will explore some of the most disturbing true life cases, solved and unsolved, over the last 140 years here in Toronto. From old Sayer Street in the old Ward to Hospital Row. In areas that one would find quiet, and comfortable, there are demons hiding, some in plain sight. Like HH Holmes said just before he dropped through the trap door of the gallows at Moyamensing Prison; \"I always had the Devil in me.\"\n\nThis is not a **ghost** tour but a continuation of the Dark History of Toronto Series that started back in 2019 with Volume 1.\n\nThis horrific walking tour is for all levels and walkers. **But this tour is not for children under the age of 12**\n\nThe tour begins at the **Toronto Sign** in Nathan Philips Square. The tour ends at Bay and College Streets.\n\n**Please book early if you wish to attend this event in October! And Mr. Holmes will be waiting, patiently for your prompt RSVP!**\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**","venue":{"name":"Nathan Philips Square","address":"100 Queen St W, Toronto","lat":43.652283,"lng":-79.38334,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":{"amount":15,"currency":"CAD"},"group":"Toronto History Walks","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/4/3/8/highres_505881560.jpeg"}